From: dagu
Subject: [PATCH] kms: do not queue on pending_page_flip when deadline is off

Against mutter 50.1 (Ubuntu libmutter-18 50.1-0ubuntu2.2).

update_ready() queues the update when pending_page_flip is set,
even if is_using_deadline_timer() is FALSE (KMS thread
SCHED_OTHER). schedule_process() in that state only
g_warning_once() and does not flush pending_update.

Race on identity GTK: handle_update for N+1 runs on the KMS
thread before drmHandleEvent has cleared pending_page_flip for
N. The update sits in pending_update until the next maybe_post
(65-200 ms). drmModeAtomicCommit is then late; dpu_enc_kickoff
follows immediately. wait_flush in the hole is 0-6 ms.

Live ELF (objdump of /proc/<pid>/map_files):
  0x1bd7d4  cbnz w0,#pending_page_flip,queue  → nop
  falls through to do_process_update (0x1bd7d8)

Do not also poke schedule_process 0x1bce48; that flush was worse.

---
 src/backends/native/meta-kms-impl-device.c | 9 +++++----
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/backends/native/meta-kms-impl-device.c b/src/backends/native/meta-kms-impl-device.c
index 0000000..dagu0006 100644
--- a/src/backends/native/meta-kms-impl-device.c
+++ b/src/backends/native/meta-kms-impl-device.c
@@ -2034,8 +2034,9 @@ meta_kms_impl_device_update_ready (MetaThreadImpl  *impl,
 
   maybe_set_kms_ready_time (crtc_frame, update);
 
-  if ((want_deadline_timer || crtc_frame->pending_page_flip) &&
-      !meta_kms_update_get_mode_sets (update))
+  /* Deadline off: pending_page_flip must not queue. schedule_process
+   * will not flush that queue. Kernel serializes the next atomic. */
+  if (want_deadline_timer && !meta_kms_update_get_mode_sets (update))
     {
       if (crtc_frame->pending_page_flip)
         {
